<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24563" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intŏlĕrantĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f.
		intolerans. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>impatience</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intolerantia, cum injurias, quae sunt ferendae,
					non toleramus, neque ferimus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 17, 19, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Pass.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Unendurableness</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sitis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Oros. 5, 15</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Esp., of conduct, <i>insufferableness</i>, <i>insolence</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">superbia atque intolerantia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Clu. 40 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Agr. 2, 13, 33</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">morum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 51</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fletoris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. 2
					Macc. 9, 10</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
